Two things to know before changing anything here:

  * The .as files compile at SERVER BOOT, not at docker build. A green build
    proves nothing — run server/test/boot-test.sh against the image. Warsow's
    AngelScript is stricter than Warfork's, so boot Warsow first.

  * ONE source tree feeds BOTH games. The Warfork image copies these scripts
    and applies warfork/scriptpatches/patch-scripts-as2024.py on top (AS2024
    `.length` -> `.length()`, and stubbing the Client demo methods Warfork
    lacks). Do not fork the tree to accommodate one engine.

Upstream is NOT stock-engine-clean either: c63f9f3 itself calls RS_QueryPjState,
RS_ResetPjState (hrace/player.as) and G_RemoveProjectiles (hrace.as), all of
which come from racesow engine patches rather than stock Warsow/Warfork.
